 "note_en": "不冻港 \"ice-free port\" is built as 不 + verb + noun: 不 negates the verb (冻 \"freeze\"), and the whole phrase describes the noun, \"a port that doesn't freeze.\" The same pattern gives 不夜城 \"a city that never sleeps\" (literally \"a not-night city\"). English needs a relative clause or a compound like \"ice-free\"; Chinese just stacks the three characters.",
